{title: 350 - Blest Be the Tie That Binds}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #350 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 350}
{meta: category Christian Church - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]Blest be the [C]tie that [F]binds [F7]our [Bb]hearts in [F]Christian [C]love;
[C]The fel[C7]low[F]ship of [C]kin[C7]dred [F]minds [Bb]is [F]like [Bb]to [F]that [C7]a[F]bove.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F][C]Before [F][F7]our [Bb][F]Father's [C]throne
[C][C7][F]we [C][C7]pour [F][Bb][F]our [Bb][F]ardent [C7][F]prayers;
[F]our [C]fears, [F]our [F7]hopes, [Bb]our [F]aims [C]are one,
[C][C7][F]our [C][C7]comforts [F][Bb][F]and [Bb][F]our [C7][F]cares.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F][C]We [F]share [F7][Bb]each [F]other's [C]woes,
[C][C7][F]our [C][C7][F]mutual [Bb][F][Bb]burdens [F][C7][F]bear;
[F][C]and [F]often [F7]for [Bb]each [F]other [C]flows
[C][C7][F][C]the [C7][F][Bb][F]sympathizing [Bb][F][C7][F]tear.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[F][C]When [F][F7]we [Bb][F]asunder [C]part,
[C][C7][F]it [C][C7]gives [F][Bb][F]us [Bb][F]inward [C7][F]pain;
[F]but [C]we [F]shall [F7]still [Bb]be [F]joined [C]in heart,
[C][C7][F]and [C][C7]hope [F][Bb][F]to [Bb][F]meet [C7][F]again.
{end_of_verse}
